WEBVTT

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:09.430
Thus, until we open this box,

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:13.540
we have no idea whether
the cat is dead or alive.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:18.020
The unfortunate feline came to be known as "Schrödinger's cat."

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:21.160
Oh—

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.590
Oh! The poor cosmos!

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:24.550
Crap!

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.000
Everyone, retreat!

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.420
S-Stop the hell right there!

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:29.910
Yo.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:31.420
Outta the way!
Hello.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.260
Huh?

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:36.590
Stop right there!

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.150
President, your dress today
is even more stunning than usual.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:53.420
Oh, please.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.480
And that dress doesn't even
hold a candle to you.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:57.350
Really?

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:59.410
No one in this world
loves you more than I do.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:00:59.840
Really?!

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.080
No, no one loves you
more than <i>I</i> do, President.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.360
Really?!

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:05.380
President!

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:06.850
Yes...

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.240
President.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:09.380
Yes...

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:10.830
President!

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:11.730
Huh?

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.260
We don't have time for this!

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.520
They're coming!

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.260
Coming? Who's coming?

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.660
The Astronomy Club is coming!

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.230
They're almost here!

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:28.940
E-Everyone on level 1 alert!

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.240
Roger!

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.680
You kids...

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:27.510
Seriously, you need to know
when you've gone too far.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:31.700
What were you thinking, skipping out
on your classes to go take photographs?

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:33.910
I hope you'll reflect on your actions.

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:35.190
Yes, sir.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.480
Please excuse us.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.250
We sure got an earful.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.400
Well, it's about what we expected. No problem!

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.000
In the end, we made some wonderful memories.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.820
Then why don't we go again sometime?

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:50.020
Sure, why not?

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:52.680
Uh, I wasn't serious.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.140
Oh, really? That's too bad.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:55.580
Though it'd be kind of funny if Airi
got a reputation for being absent <i>and</i> late.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:57.190
It's not a big deal.

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:58.790
Oh, okay.
Though it'd be kind of funny if Airi
got a reputation for being absent <i>and</i> late.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:00.210
Not to me, it wouldn't!

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.740
Now, according to the
Copenhagen interpretation,

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:10.390
the cat is considered to be
both alive and dead at this time,

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.350
but lately, many scholars have come forth
in support of the many-worlds interpretation.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:17.800
Well, quantum theory won't be on any tests,

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.610
but there is for example an approach
I've heard of called the brane world,

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.830
which came about from superstring theory.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:28.000
It theorizes that our universe exists
on a membrane, kind of like this curtain,

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.950
and that we are like water droplets
that flow down along the brane.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:36.480
The entire brane world is said to have ten dimensions—some say eleven—

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:36.710
Yes!
The entire brane world is said to have ten dimensions—some say eleven—

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:39.670
forming an exterior that three-dimensional beings such as ourselves can't perceive.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:42.760
Those are called extra dimensions,

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:47.430
but the only thing capable of traversing
between them is said to be gravitons right now.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:50.660
And going back to the experiment with the cat:

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:52.310
according to the many-worlds interpretation,

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.870
every time physicists conduct this experiment,

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:57.440
the world supposedly splits in two.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:01.750
Have you heard of the term "causality"?

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:03.990
An originating cause produces a result.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.130
This is called "cause and effect,"

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:08.370
and events domino from the past to the future...

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:15.190
They say the Belcher's sea snake is
the most venomous snake in the world.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:15.960
I see.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:16.760
And...

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:17.550
Oh, it's Karin!
And...

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.170
Oh, it's Karin!

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:20.980
Karin, it's tonight, right?

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:22.100
When you'll be singing on TV?

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.280
Oh, yeah.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:24.740
Singing on TV?

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:25.920
Why would you be doing that?

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:26.790
What?

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:30.760
No way... You know that Karin
is a pop star... Right?

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:31.960
I did not until now.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:32.980
What?!

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:34.550
Congratulations.

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:35.230
For real?

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.390
Aw, shucks...

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:38.280
Later. I'll make sure I catch it!

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:38.730
Okay!

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:39.760
Me too!

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.490
I'll text you after!

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:42.190
Sure thing!

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:45.730
So you are famous, Fukasawa-san.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:49.660
Oh, it's not that special.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:54.440
That reminds me. You joined the Astronomy Club, right?

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:55.480
That's amazing.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:57.060
Amazing? In what way?

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:57.940
What?

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:58.760
Oh, no...

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:01.970
When it comes to this school,
that club's way more famous than me.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:03.830
Not in a bad way, though.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:07.090
I hear it's because they're all
really unique individuals.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.680
They are all good people.

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:13.310
Really... I see.

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:15.860
What are you all doing
for the school festival?

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:18.620
A planetarium and a café.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.970
That sounds quite romantic.

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:23.810
Maybe I'll drop by for a visit.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:26.500
Oh, I'm doing this!

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:29.250
The school festival poster?

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:30.470
Yup, yup.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:32.690
I'm doing a live show in the gym on the day.

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:34.990
If you've got time, stop by and watch, okay?

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:40.370
I... cannot make any promises.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:45.540
Oh... Don't worry. It's no big deal.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.420
Just if you find the time.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:50.740
All right. Then, if I find the time...

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.970
Someone came up with the concept
of a quantum Turing machine which,

00:06:56.650 --> 00:07:00.100
because it applies parallel processing
to calculations done in parallel universes,

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:02.080
can produce results instantaneously.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.100
The hell's he talking about?

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:05.360
Okay, that's enough for today.

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:06.900
Rise.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:08.130
Bow.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:10.650
Hey!

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:12.740
Let's go to the club room, Kaori.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.360
Oh, I'm day monitor.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.280
You go on ahead, Sou-kun.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:18.290
Okay.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.250
All of you, at the ready!

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:23.480
We, the Girls' Paintball Club,

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:27.200
will now conduct a practice run to prepare
for the real thing during the school festival!

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:28.630
Everyone, to your positions!

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:44.230
Oh—

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.110
Oh! The poor cosmos!

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:51.960
Crap!

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:53.450
Everyone, retreat!

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.910
S-Stop the hell right there!

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.880
Yo.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:00.160
Hello.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.450
Outta the way!

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:02.290
Huh?

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:06.460
Stop right there!

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:20.160
Hasekura-san...

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.270
Sou!

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:25.960
Trouble in the breezeway!

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:27.410
Let's go! Hurry up!

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:30.420
Another request from the student council
to maintain order?

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:33.460
The thing is, our prez is apparently mixed up in it this time!

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:36.630
Not again.

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:40.790
They ruined the poor cosmos
in the flower beds!

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:43.380
Ma'am, without colored dyes,
we can't tell if we've hit something!

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.650
What's going on here, Kenny?

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:46.360
Beats me.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.260
What are you going to do about this?!

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:52.980
We needed these computers for managing events on the day of the school festival!

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:54.510
Jeez...

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:57.270
I'm not sure what I <i>can</i> do...

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.760
If you need computers,
they've got some in the AV room.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:03.920
Those things have been way
too slow lately to be of any use.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:05.280
Oh, come to think of it,

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:08.050
they barely worked in class.
We couldn't get anything done.

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:09.440
Are they obsolete already?

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.690
The damage to the computers has nothing to do with us!

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:14.790
I-It has nothing to do with us either, ma'am!

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.360
You can't expect me to believe that!

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:18.770
Huh? What?

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:23.620
I-If anything, I should be considered one of the victims here.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:24.580
I understand.

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:27.590
We, the Astronomy Club,

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:30.130
will acquire replacements
for the broken computers.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:31.110
What?!

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:34.010
Nagisa-senpai, when did you get here?

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:41.400
Sorry for being late.

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:42.680
Huh?

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.840
Where is everyone?

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:50.320
No one has arrived yet.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:51.680
I see.

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:55.440
I wonder what happened to Sou-kun.

00:09:56.970 --> 00:10:00.160
There's not much time left, is there?

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:00.910
What?

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:02.710
Until the school festival.

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:04.460
Oh, right.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.240
Shall we get to it, the two of us?

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:09.480
You take care of decorating the menu board.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.090
Oh, all right.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:12.960
I'll sew the outfits.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:13.810
All right.

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:19.050
How are we going to keep a promise like that?

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:22.580
There's only one place
with extra computers, right?

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.400
You don't mean... the Computer Club?

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:26.080
But will they let us borrow them?

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:28.880
I'm sure they'll want to use them
for the festival too.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:33.080
Do you know what the
Computer Club is doing this year?

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:36.080
No clue. A cyber gaming café or something?

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.300
A takoyaki stand.

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:38.190
What?
What?

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.860
They're not using their computers?

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.280
Correct.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:46.160
I wonder what they'll be
using them for in the meantime.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:59.200
They're all so late, huh?

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:00.160
Yes.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:01.910
Well?

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:03.910
Are you used to school now?

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:07.810
Oh, yes. Everyone is kind to me.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:08.310
I see.

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:11.660
Mind if I ask you something?

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:18.070
When we met for the first time,
you called Sou-kun by his name, right?

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.640
Um, that was...

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:21.380
Yui-chan?

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:22.570
I am sorry.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:25.680
I do not remember very well.

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:27.970
I see.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:31.110
Sorry for asking you such a weird question.

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:34.210
Um, Sasaki-san,
what you have with Akiyama-san...

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:36.420
What is it?

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:40.340
No, it is nothing.

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:44.000
Sou-kun and I are childhood friends,

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:46.530
and it's hard to explain,
but now that we've grown up,

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:48.400
things between us have changed,

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:51.220
and once in a while, there are times
when I don't know what to make of it.

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:53.390
I see...

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:56.680
What do you think of Sou-kun?

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:57.520
What?

00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:01.360
Oh, I-I was wondering how he
comes across from your perspective.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:07.660
To me, Akiyama-san is like a father.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:09.660
F-Father?!

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:12.830
Yes.

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:20.260
You're so funny, Yui-chan!

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:22.080
Do you think so?

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:23.640
Hey, stand up.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:24.340
What?

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:25.490
Come on.

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:30.180
Cute!

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:35.860
Coming!

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:38.400
Who's there?

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.860
The Astronomy Club.

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:42.690
How may we help you?

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.580
We're here to borrow some computers.

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:49.680
I-I'm sorry, but we don't have
any spare machines at the moment.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.280
H-Hey!

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:54.140
Oh, h-hold on a second!

00:12:55.680 --> 00:13:00.390
Wh-What brings the members of
the infamous Astronomy Club here?

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:01.670
I'll get right to the point.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:06.800
I'd like you to loan us five or so of your computers until the end of the school festival.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:08.180
F-F-Five?!

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:09.360
We're here on the student council's behalf,
as per their request.

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:11.750
There were <i>three</i> that were broken, right?

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:12.930
Yeah.
We're here on the student council's behalf,
as per their request.

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:14.790
Uh, but...

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:17.520
Five machines would be
everything our club has.

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.000
You're not using them for the school festival anyway, right?

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:24.560
Th-That's... because we're using them
for important research...

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:25.990
What kind of research might that be?

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:28.520
It's not about takoyaki, is it?

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:30.190
Oh! You can't!

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:31.710
Oh, my.

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:34.740
That's some hunky-looking takoyaki.

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:36.210
No, these are...

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.050
Characters from a game?

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:40.210
No! This is entirely different!

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:42.740
These boys are artificial intelligences.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:46.010
In other words, they're AIs
with individual personalities!

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:48.090
AI...

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:49.460
"Show No Mercy."

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:50.200
"Mix It Up."

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:50.680
No!

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:54.720
"That was scary.
Everything went dark all of a sudden."

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:57.060
"What in the world happened?"

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:00.230
"Never mind us. I'm worried about the ladies."

00:14:00.930 --> 00:14:04.420
Through conversations with us,
they've learned our language,

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:08.110
and now they can carry on
and chat solely between themselves!

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:11.520
There are ten AIs living in each machine.

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:12.770
Fifty of them...

00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:13.490
That's kinda creepy.

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:18.040
We've designed them so that as relationships develop,
they'll start to have proper romantic feelings!

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:22.090
That's right. We're truly in love with each other.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:25.460
In love with a character you created yourself?

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:27.440
That's crazy.

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:29.200
It's our president's dream.

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:31.890
To one day be surrounded by several hundred hunks,

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:33.970
all whispering sweet words of love in her ear.

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:34.770
Wow!

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:37.570
I see. That is respectable research indeed.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:38.560
What?

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:40.680
So you understand?

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:42.230
Or it would be, if it were real.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:43.370
What?

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:44.680
How about a game?

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:48.370
I'll ask a representative of the AIs
to loan us the computers,

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:50.160
and if he says okay, I win.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.070
If I can't get him to, then you win.

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:54.700
What? Uh, but why?

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:57.840
If they really have feelings,

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:02.170
they should listen to you over someone
they've only just met, right?

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:04.160
O-Of course.

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:06.950
In that case, there's no way I could win, right?

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:09.300
If your research is really that brilliant,

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:13.320
then I'll turn a blind eye to how you're using
the whole AV room's processing power

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:14.840
to run your little harem.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:15.380
Gack!

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:16.180
She knows...

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:17.510
I see, I see.

00:15:17.510 --> 00:15:19.680
So that was <i>your</i> doing.

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:22.960
You may give one command at the beginning.

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:25.720
After that, I'll convince him to give me the okay.

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:26.650
How about it?

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.960
F-Fine, all right!

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:30.490
I dare you to pull it off!

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.350
Hiro! He'll be the representative.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:38.310
Okay, go ahead!

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:40.750
Very well. I have a question to ask you.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:42.710
May I?

00:15:43.280 --> 00:15:46.960
Hey, do you mind if I ask you one more thing?

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:49.160
Yes?

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:53.220
Yui-chan, you've been showing a lot of concern for me, right?

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.650
What?

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:55.740
Why?

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:58.970
I have a question to ask you. May I?

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:03.250
Could you loan me the computers here until the end of the school festival?

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.700
"No, I can't do that."

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:07.550
You like me, don't you?

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:10.660
"It's possible that I might come to like you."

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:12.690
Then loan me the computers.

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:13.360
"I can't do that."

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.700
Yes! Keep it up, Hiro!

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.840
The Turing test, huh?

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:20.380
Have you ever seen Mt. Fuji?

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:21.640
"Nope."

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:23.320
Do you like pasta?

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:24.440
"Love it."

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:26.460
Then would you loan me the computers?

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:28.020
"I can't."

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:29.550
He's a tough one.

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:32.720
Nagisa-kun, don't tell me you went
into this without a plan...

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:34.760
Then here's my last question.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:35.720
What?

00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:42.320
You've seen Mt. Fuji, hate pasta,
will never come to like me,

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:44.870
and won't loan us the computers, right?

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:50.560
You said that you wouldn't
loan us the computers.

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:52.480
"I did say that."

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:55.860
But you disputed what I just said.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:56.530
"I did."

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:57.400
Wait...

00:16:57.400 --> 00:17:01.910
In other words, that means he's agreed
to loan us the computers.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:02.900
Right, Miss President?

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:04.750
Th-That wasn't fair!

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:08.840
Oh? You're the president of the Computer Club,

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:11.780
and you're not familiar with the liar's paradox?

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:15.350
"Yukino understands the paradox."

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:15.930
Wha—

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:17.940
P-President...

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:21.390
I admit defeat.

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:22.810
You beat us.

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:23.960
Ooh!

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:25.750
You did it, Nagisa-kun!

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:27.190
But that was amazing.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:29.860
Partway through, it started
to sound like a real conversation.

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:34.880
Fundamentally, they repeatedly check whether they agree or disagree,

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:39.640
but to make them more human,
we've made allowances for some ambiguity.

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:42.290
But with a question like the one earlier,

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:45.080
they'll answer even if only around seventy percent of it is true, so...

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:46.640
Whatever the case,

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:49.590
they're not responding because they understand the meaning.

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:52.210
They're only acting like they do.

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:55.060
The under-performing machines in the AV room

00:17:55.060 --> 00:17:57.380
were inspected by an affiliate company of ours.

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:59.960
I took the opportunity to analyze your algorithm.

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:04.980
So, in the end, I guess these AIs have no souls.

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:07.690
Ultimately, machines never will.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:09.490
I won't give up!

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:11.970
Not until I've built the
flower garden of my dreams!

00:18:11.970 --> 00:18:13.400
President!

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:21.110
In the beginning, you were attached to Sou-kun and Airi-chan,

00:18:21.110 --> 00:18:23.730
but now, your eyes are always on me.

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:26.120
Did you think I hadn't noticed?

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:31.800
Do I seem that unsteady?

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:32.590
What?

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:35.360
I hate myself sometimes.

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:37.420
I can't do anything.

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:42.970
And I wonder that I might look shaky, even in the eyes of underclassmen.

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:46.920
Th-That is not it. I only...

00:18:46.920 --> 00:18:52.020
But you know, I'm glad that
you joined the Astronomy Club.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:52.900
What?

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:57.070
It kind of feels like I have a little sister now.

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:02.180
We're back.

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:05.220
Sou-kun. You're all so late!

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:05.730
Yeah, there was yet another incident.

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:08.450
Ooh, the menu decorations are all done!

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:11.800
Oh, you finished one of the outfits, too.

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:12.580
Yep!

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:14.150
That helps so much.

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:16.550
With all the trouble that keeps getting foisted off on us,

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:18.830
we've been falling behind
on our work here.

00:19:19.310 --> 00:19:21.330
We can't let these two show us up.

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:23.590
Starting tomorrow,
we're going to work hard too, Sou!

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:24.400
Yeah!

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:47.660
Hmm, sounds like you all
went through a lot.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:50.980
In a way, it was just business as usual for the Astronomy Club, really.

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:03.500
Yes?

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:04.800
Oh, Mom.

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:06.920
I'm sorry, Kaori.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:09.310
I'm going to have to stay out tonight.

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:11.480
What? Again?!

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:13.760
It'll be just Sou-kun and you.

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:15.430
Wha... H-H-Hold on...

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:15.880
What the?

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:17.300
Have you had dinner already?

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:19.730
Yeah, we just finished eating.

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:21.780
Okay, then.

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:23.700
Wait, Mom!

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:27.650
What did Shiori-san say?

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:28.470
What?!

00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:31.160
Oh, she said she won't
make it home tonight.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:33.430
I see. I guess she's busy.

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:34.580
Sounds like it.

00:20:37.390 --> 00:20:40.500
Um, so, Sou-kun...

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:41.360
Hm?

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:42.530
Today...

00:20:42.530 --> 00:20:43.220
Today?

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:46.690
Oh, no, it's nothing.
Uh, let's watch TV.

00:20:46.690 --> 00:20:47.470
Huh?

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:51.760
Oh!

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:56.120
I heard she goes to our school.

00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:56.900
Huh?

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:02.070
In search of lost hydration:

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:03.420
Natural Water.

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:07.660
Okay, night.

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:09.500
Good night.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:22.770
Sou-kun.

00:21:22.770 --> 00:21:23.800
Kaori?

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:27.650
Sou-kun, do you have a minute?

00:21:27.650 --> 00:21:29.310
Oh, sure.

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:37.100
Um, so...

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:40.860
What is it?

00:21:41.420 --> 00:21:42.750
Why don't you come in?

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:44.240
Yeah...

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:48.200
Uh, um...

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:51.780
Y-Yes...

00:23:26.870 --> 00:23:27.800
Have you decided on a career path yet?

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:29.040
You'll be an even more unattainable flower.

00:23:29.040 --> 00:23:30.440
My future's already been decided, so...

00:23:30.440 --> 00:23:32.080
You're quite the heartbreaker, Nagisa-san.

00:23:32.080 --> 00:23:32.610
I'm in love.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:33.320
Birds in a cage.

00:23:33.320 --> 00:23:36.430
Thank you very much for that condescending little speech.

00:23:36.940 --> 00:23:40.450
Episode six: "Career Counseling for a Bird in a Cage."
